    "title": "What Happened to Morgan Metzer From Gaslit by My Husband?",
    "text": "Two years after Gaslit By My Husband: The Morgan Metzer Story premiered on Lifetime, the film has gained a surge in popularity with its release on Netflix. The story of Morgan Metzer has generated significant interest as the film has gained attention on Netflix.Fans are now eager to learn more about the real Morgan Metzer and where she currently is.Where is Morgan Metzer now?Morgan and Rodney Metzer’s story was the basis of the Lifetime film, Gaslit By My Husband: The Morgan Metzer Story. Jana Kramer and Austin Nichols starred as the couple in the film.The film follows events surrounding the troubled marriage between Rodney and Morgan. It also explores how the situation eventually culminated in a shocking incident one night.Morgan Metzer suffered years of physical and mental trauma during her marriage to Rodney Metzer. He reportedly engaged in repeated gaslighting, used their twin children as leverage against her, and sexually assaulted her over the years.In 2020, Morgan finally filed for divorce from Rodney. The divorce was finalized the same year. However, Rodney reportedly continued attempting to reconcile, including faking cancer (per 48 Hours).After a brief period of contact, Morgan asked Rodney to leave on New Year’s Eve in 2020. However, in the early hours of New Year’s Day 2021, Morgan was assaulted at her home by a masked intruder. She was zip-tied, beaten, and sexually assaulted. Investigators later identified Rodney as the attacker. Following the investigation, Rodney was sentenced to 25 years in prison.Morgan faced challenges while recovering from the trauma, but decided to rebuild her life. She began attending therapy and worked to move forward from the experience. Currently, her focus is on raising her two children. Moreover, Morgan is using her experience to help others facing similar situations.“I’m trying to raise awareness for … narcissism and gaslighting,” she explained to 48 Hours (via EW). “I want to help women realize they’re in a situation before it gets too bad.”She added, “If I don’t take the bad that came of this, that I feel God wants me to do, it’s like, why did it happen. It would have happened for no reason. I’ve got to take the pain and turn that into something that’s powerful to help women.”Gaslit By My Husband: The Morgan Metzer Story is now streaming on Netflix.The post What Happened to Morgan Metzer From Gaslit by My Husband? appeared first on ComingSoon.net - Movie Trailers, TV & Streaming News, and More.",
